<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="false">
  <code><![CDATA[
breed [ bases base ]                   ;; defended targets
breed [ drones drone ]                 ;; attackers: lethal (red) or decoy (yellow)
breed [ interceptors interceptor ]     ;; defensive drones launched by the bases
breed [ effects effect ]               ;; short-lived hit / miss markers (visual only)

patches-own [
  ground-color                         ;; map colour in clear weather
]

bases-own [
  health                               ;; 100 at start; the base is destroyed at 0
  ammo                                 ;; interceptors ready to launch (0 to 10)
  reload-timer                         ;; ticks until the next interceptor is ready
  launch-cooldown                      ;; ticks until the base can launch again
]

drones-own [
  decoy?                               ;; true = unarmed decoy, false = lethal drone
  target                               ;; the base this drone flies at
  speed                                ;; patches per tick
  launched                             ;; tick of launch (to find the drones of the new wave)
]

interceptors-own [
  target                               ;; the drone being chased
  fuel                                 ;; ticks of flight left
]

effects-own [
  lifespan                             ;; ticks until the marker disappears
]

globals [
  raining?                             ;; current weather (the dynamic environment)
  wave                                 ;; number of waves launched so far
  wave-timer                           ;; ticks until the next wave
  lethal-hits                          ;; lethal drones that reached a base
  bases-destroyed
  lethal-shot-down                     ;; interceptor kills on lethal drones
  decoys-shot-down                     ;; interceptor kills on decoys (wasted interceptors)
  radar-drawn-for                      ;; visual only: number of bases when the radar ranges were drawn
]

;; Fixed constants of the model
to-report magazine-size     report 10 end
to-report lethal-cost       report 100 end     ;; a decoy costs decoy-cost (slider)
to-report warhead-damage    report 34 end      ;; three hits destroy a base
to-report interceptor-speed report 1.6 * attacker-speed end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------- setup --

to setup
  clear-all
  set raining? false
  set wave-timer 5                     ;; the first wave launches after 5 ticks
  setup-map
  setup-bases
  show-radar-ranges
  update-base-looks
  reset-ticks
end

to setup-map
  ask patches [
    set ground-color zone-color
    set pcolor ground-color
  ]
end

to-report zone-color  ;; patch reporter
  report (ifelse-value
    staging-area?        [ 14 ]        ;; attacker staging area along the edges (dark red)
    distancexy 0 0 > 30  [ 2 ]         ;; neutral airspace (dark grey)
                         [ 103 ])      ;; defended homeland in the middle (navy)
end

;; Patch reporter (only for the map colours): true outside a square with rounded corners,
;; whose straight sides run 6 patches inside the world edges and whose corners are arcs of radius 16.
to-report staging-area?
  let x-out max list 0 (abs pxcor - 42)   ;; how far the patch is past the straight part of the sides
  let y-out max list 0 (abs pycor - 42)
  report x-out * x-out + y-out * y-out >= 16 * 16
end

;; number-of-bases bases in the homeland, each placed as far as possible from the
;; others (the best of 100 random candidate spots).
to setup-bases
  let homeland patches with [ distancexy 0 0 <= 24 ]
  ;; let homeland patches with [ pxcor >= 8 and pxcor <= 54 and abs pycor <= 52 ]   ;; FRONT VERSION
  repeat number-of-bases [
    let candidates n-of 100 homeland
    let spot ifelse-value any? bases
      [ max-one-of candidates [ distance-to-nearest-base ] ]
      [ one-of candidates ]
    ask spot [
      sprout-bases 1 [
        set shape "house"
        set color cyan + 1
        set size 4
        set health 100
        set ammo magazine-size
        set reload-timer base-reload-time
        set launch-cooldown 0
      ]
    ]
  ]
end

to-report distance-to-nearest-base  ;; patch reporter
  report min [ distance myself ] of bases
end

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------- go --

to go
  if simulation-over? [
    ask effects [ die ]                ;; no hit/miss markers left on screen at the end
    stop
  ]
  launch-waves
  update-weather
  reload-bases
  launch-interceptors
  move-drones
  move-interceptors
  drones-hit-bases
  fade-effects
  update-base-looks
  if count bases < radar-drawn-for [ show-radar-ranges ]   ;; a base was destroyed: its radar is gone
  tick
end

;; A wave is launched every wave-interval ticks until total-waves have been sent.
to launch-waves
  set wave-timer wave-timer - 1
  if wave-timer <= 0 and wave < total-waves [
    launch-wave
    set wave wave + 1
    set wave-timer wave-interval
  ]
end

;; Budget split: decoy-ratio % of the budget buys decoys, the rest buys lethal drones.
;; The drones of each wave are dealt out evenly over the bases.
to launch-wave
  let decoy-budget wave-budget * decoy-ratio / 100
  let n-decoys round (decoy-budget / decoy-cost)
  let n-lethal max list 1 round ((wave-budget - decoy-budget) / lethal-cost)
  create-drones n-lethal [ setup-drone false ]
  create-drones n-decoys [ setup-drone true ]
  let new-wave drones with [ launched = ticks ]
  deal-out-targets new-wave with [ not decoy? ]    ;; every base gets the same number of warheads
  deal-out-targets new-wave with [ decoy? ]        ;; ... and of decoys
end

to setup-drone [ is-decoy? ]  ;; drone procedure
  set decoy? is-decoy?
  set launched ticks
  set speed attacker-speed * (0.95 + random-float 0.1)   ;; +/- 5% so the swarm spreads out
  set shape "airplane"
  set color ifelse-value decoy? [ yellow + 1 ] [ red ]
  set size ifelse-value decoy? [ 1.8 ] [ 2.2 ]
  let angle random-float 360           ;; somewhere on the staging circle
  setxy (60 * sin angle) (60 * cos angle)
  ;; setxy -56 (random-float 100 - 50)  ;; FRONT VERSION: somewhere along the staging line in the west
end

;; The bases take turns, like dealing cards: 1st drone -> 1st base, 2nd -> 2nd base, ...
to deal-out-targets [ group ]
  let targets sort bases
  let i 0
  foreach sort group [ d ->
    ask d [
      set target item (i mod length targets) targets
      face target
    ]
    set i i + 1
  ]
end

;; Dynamic environment: the weather switches at random between clear and rain.
;; A shower ends with 2% chance per tick, so it lasts about 50 ticks on average.
to update-weather
  let was-raining? raining?
  ifelse raining?
    [ if random-float 100 < 2 [ set raining? false ] ]
    [ if random-float 100 < rain-chance [ set raining? true ] ]
  if raining? != was-raining? [ show-weather ]
end

to show-weather  ;; while it rains the whole map is slightly darker and "RAIN" shows at the top
  ask patches [ set pcolor ifelse-value raining? [ ground-color - 1 ] [ ground-color ] ]
  ask patch 60 60 [ set plabel ifelse-value raining? [ "RAIN" ] [ "" ] ]
end

;; A base below a full magazine gains one interceptor every base-reload-time ticks.
to reload-bases
  ask bases with [ ammo < magazine-size ] [
    set reload-timer reload-timer - 1
    if reload-timer <= 0 [
      set ammo ammo + 1
      set reload-timer base-reload-time
    ]
  ]
end

;; A base with ammo launches one interceptor at a drone inside its radar range that
;; no interceptor is chasing yet (the bases do not fire twice at the same drone).
;; With probability sensor-discrimination it recognises the lethal drones and aims
;; at the nearest one; otherwise it aims at the nearest drone, which may be a decoy.
to launch-interceptors
  ask bases [
    if launch-cooldown > 0 [ set launch-cooldown launch-cooldown - 1 ]
    let in-range not-chased (drones in-radius detection-radius)
    if ammo > 0 and launch-cooldown = 0 and any? in-range [
      let lethal-in-range in-range with [ not decoy? ]
      let chosen ifelse-value (random-float 100 < sensor-discrimination and any? lethal-in-range)
        [ min-one-of lethal-in-range [ distance myself ] ]
        [ min-one-of in-range [ distance myself ] ]
      hatch-interceptors 1 [
        set target chosen
        set fuel 75
        set shape "arrow"
        set color sky + 1
        set size 1.8
        set label ""                   ;; do not inherit the base's ammo label
        face target
        show-chase
      ]
      set ammo ammo - 1
      set launch-cooldown scramble-cooldown-ticks
    ]
  ]
end

;; Drones fly straight at their base; if it was destroyed they head for the nearest one left.
to move-drones
  ask drones [
    if target = nobody [ set target min-one-of bases [ distance myself ] ]
    ifelse target = nobody or not can-move? speed
      [ die ]
      [ face target
        fd speed ]
  ]
end

;; Interceptors chase their drone (or, if it is gone, the nearest drone nobody is chasing).
;; Out of fuel, the interceptor is lost.
to move-interceptors
  ask interceptors [
    set fuel fuel - 1
    if target = nobody [
      set target min-one-of not-chased (drones in-radius 25) [ distance myself ]
      if target != nobody [ show-chase ]
    ]
    ifelse fuel <= 0 or target = nobody or not can-move? interceptor-speed [
      mark "dot" gray
      die
    ] [
      face target
      fd interceptor-speed
      if distance target <= 1.8 [ engage target ]
    ]
  ]
end

;; On contact the interceptor rolls for a kill, which is less likely in rain.
;; Hit or miss, the interceptor is used up.
to engage [ drone-hit ]  ;; interceptor procedure
  let kill-chance intercept-accuracy * (ifelse-value raining? [ 1 - rain-penalty / 100 ] [ 1 ])
  ifelse random-float 100 < kill-chance [
    ifelse [ decoy? ] of drone-hit [
      set decoys-shot-down decoys-shot-down + 1
      mark "star" white
    ] [
      set lethal-shot-down lethal-shot-down + 1
      mark "star" yellow
    ]
    ask drone-hit [ die ]
  ] [
    mark "x" gray + 2
  ]
  die
end

to drones-hit-bases
  ask drones [
    if target != nobody and distance target <= 2.2 [ hit-target ]
  ]
end

to hit-target  ;; drone procedure: a lethal drone damages its base, a decoy only by decoy-damage
  ifelse decoy? [
    mark "dot" gray
    ask target [ take-damage decoy-damage ]
  ] [
    set lethal-hits lethal-hits + 1
    mark "star" red
    ask target [ take-damage warhead-damage ]
  ]
  die
end

to take-damage [ amount ]  ;; base procedure
  set health health - amount
  if health <= 0 [
    set bases-destroyed bases-destroyed + 1
    mark "circle" orange
    die
  ]
end

to mark [ shape-name marker-color ]  ;; turtle procedure: leave a short-lived marker here
  hatch-effects 1 [
    set shape shape-name
    set color marker-color
    set size 3
    set lifespan 5
  ]
end

to fade-effects
  ask effects [
    set lifespan lifespan - 1
    if lifespan <= 0 [ die ]
  ]
end

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------ visuals --
;; These procedures only change how the model looks. with-local-randomness makes
;; sure they do not use up random numbers, so the simulation runs exactly as without them.

to show-radar-ranges  ;; the ground inside a base's radar range is one shade lighter
  set radar-drawn-for count bases
  with-local-randomness [
    ask patches [ set ground-color zone-color ]
    ask bases [ ask patches in-radius detection-radius [ set ground-color zone-color + 1 ] ]
    ask patches [ set pcolor ifelse-value raining? [ ground-color - 1 ] [ ground-color ] ]
  ]
end

to update-base-looks  ;; colour shows the health of a base, the label its interceptors left
  with-local-randomness [
    ask bases [
      set color (ifelse-value health > 66 [ cyan + 1 ] health > 32 [ orange ] [ red ])
      set label ammo
    ]
  ]
end

to show-chase  ;; interceptor procedure: a thin line to the drone it chases (it vanishes with either)
  create-link-to target [ set color sky + 2 ]   ;; light blue, visible on the navy homeland too
end

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- reporters --

to-report total-base-health
  report sum [ health ] of bases
end

to-report not-chased [ candidates ]  ;; the drones among candidates that no interceptor is chasing yet
  report candidates with [ not any? interceptors with [ target = myself ] ]
end

;; The run ends when all bases are destroyed, or when every wave has been
;; launched and no drone is left (500 ticks is a safety limit).
to-report simulation-over?
  report not any? bases
    or (wave >= total-waves and not any? drones)
    or ticks >= 500
end]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="310" wrappingAllowedX="true" y="10" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="-64" height="480" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="3.75" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="true" width="480" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="63" updateMode="1" maxPxcor="63" minPxcor="-64"></view>
    <button x="10" y="10" height="35" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="90" display="setup">setup</button>
    <button x="105" y="10" height="35" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="90" display="go-once">go</button>
    <button x="200" y="10" height="35" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="90" display="go">go</button>
    <slider x="10" step="50" y="55" max="5000" width="150" display="wave-budget" height="50" min="500" direction="Horizontal" default="3750.0" variable="wave-budget"></slider>
    <slider x="155" step="2" y="55" max="100" width="150" display="decoy-ratio" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="20.0" variable="decoy-ratio" units="%"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="1" y="105" max="100" width="150" display="decoy-cost" height="50" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="15.0" variable="decoy-cost"></slider>
    <slider x="155" step="0.1" y="105" max="1.5" width="150" display="attacker-speed" height="50" min="0.5" direction="Horizontal" default="0.9" variable="attacker-speed"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="1" y="155" max="5" width="150" display="total-waves" height="50" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="2.0" variable="total-waves"></slider>
    <slider x="155" step="10" y="155" max="100" width="150" display="wave-interval" height="50" min="30" direction="Horizontal" default="60.0" variable="wave-interval"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="10" y="205" max="100" width="150" display="sensor-discrimination" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="50.0" variable="sensor-discrimination" units="%"></slider>
    <slider x="155" step="5" y="205" max="95" width="150" display="intercept-accuracy" height="50" min="30" direction="Horizontal" default="85.0" variable="intercept-accuracy" units="%"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="1" y="255" max="30" width="150" display="base-reload-time" height="50" min="2" direction="Horizontal" default="4.0" variable="base-reload-time"></slider>
    <slider x="155" step="1" y="255" max="40" width="150" display="detection-radius" height="50" min="15" direction="Horizontal" default="26.0" variable="detection-radius"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="1" y="305" max="10" width="150" display="scramble-cooldown-ticks" height="50" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="1.0" variable="scramble-cooldown-ticks"></slider>
    <slider x="155" step="0.5" y="305" max="5" width="150" display="rain-chance" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="1.0" variable="rain-chance" units="%"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="5" y="405" max="100" width="150" display="rain-penalty" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="50.0" variable="rain-penalty" units="%"></slider>
    <slider x="10" step="1" y="355" max="8" width="150" display="number-of-bases" height="50" min="2" direction="Horizontal" default="4.0" variable="number-of-bases"></slider>
    <slider x="155" step="0.1" y="355" max="10" width="150" display="decoy-damage" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.0" variable="decoy-damage"></slider>
    <monitor x="155" precision="0" y="405" height="60" fontSize="11" width="135" display="weather">ifelse-value raining? [ "rain" ] [ "clear" ]</monitor>
    <monitor x="10" precision="0" y="475" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="ticks">ticks</monitor>
    <monitor x="106" precision="0" y="475" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="bases left">count bases</monitor>
    <monitor x="202" precision="0" y="475" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="lethal hits">lethal-hits</monitor>
    <monitor x="10" precision="0" y="545" height="60" fontSize="11" width="135" display="warheads shot down">lethal-shot-down</monitor>
    <monitor x="155" precision="0" y="545" height="60" fontSize="11" width="135" display="decoys shot down">decoys-shot-down</monitor>
    <plot x="800" autoPlotX="true" yMax="400.0" autoPlotY="false" yAxis="Health" y="460" xMin="0.0" height="160" legend="false" xMax="100.0" yMin="0.0" width="300" xAxis="Ticks" display="Total Base Health">
      <setup>set-plot-y-range 0 (100 * number-of-bases)</setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Health" color="-13345367" legend="false">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plot total-base-health</update>
      </pen>
    </plot>
    <plot x="800" autoPlotX="true" yMax="15.0" autoPlotY="true" yAxis="Cumulative" y="10" xMin="0.0" height="220" legend="true" xMax="100.0" yMin="0.0" width="300" xAxis="Ticks" display="Interception Outcomes">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Warheads shot down" color="-13345367" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plot lethal-shot-down</update>
      </pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Decoys shot down" color="-1184463" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plot decoys-shot-down</update>
      </pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Lethal hits on bases" color="-2674135" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plot lethal-hits</update>
      </pen>
    </plot>
    <plot x="800" autoPlotX="false" yMax="10.0" autoPlotY="true" yAxis="Drones" y="240" xMin="0.0" height="210" legend="true" xMax="70.0" yMin="0.0" width="300" xAxis="Distance to target base" display="Incoming Drones by Distance">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen interval="5.0" mode="1" display="Decoys" color="-1184463" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>histogram [ distance target ] of drones with [ decoy? and target != nobody ]</update>
      </pen>
      <pen interval="5.0" mode="1" display="Lethal drones" color="-2674135" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>histogram [ distance target ] of drones with [ not decoy? and target != nobody ]</update>
      </pen>
    </plot>
  </widgets>
  <info>## WHAT IS IT?

A model of a defence being saturated by cheap decoy drones. For every wave, the attacker has a fixed budget and splits it between expensive lethal drones and cheap decoys. The bases defend themselves with interceptors, but each base has only a small magazine that reloads slowly, and its sensors cannot always tell a decoy from an armed drone.

**Why:** to find out how the share of the budget spent on decoys, together with the defender's ability to recognise decoys, decides whether the defence holds or collapses.

## HOW IT WORKS

**Bases** have 100 health, a magazine of 10 interceptors and a reload timer. Every tick, a base with ammo launches one interceptor at a drone within its radar range that no interceptor is chasing yet:
- with probability `sensor-discrimination` it recognises the lethal drones and aims at the nearest one;
- otherwise it aims at the nearest drone of any kind, so decoys draw fire.

**Drones** launch in waves from a circle near the dark red edges and fly straight at a base. The drones of a wave are dealt out evenly over the bases. Red drones are lethal: three hits destroy a base. Yellow drones are decoys and do no damage by default. If a drone's base is destroyed, it flies at the nearest one left.

**Interceptors** chase one drone each and roll for a kill on contact (`intercept-accuracy`). They are used up whether they hit or miss. If their drone is gone, they chase the nearest drone that nobody is chasing.

**Weather (dynamic environment):** rain showers start at random (`rain-chance`) and end with 2% probability per tick. While it rains, the map is darker and interceptors hit less often (`rain-penalty`).

**Saturation:** because the magazines are small and reload slowly, a large enough swarm empties them, and the drones that follow get through.

The run stops when all bases are destroyed or every wave is over.

## HOW TO USE IT

Press **setup**, then **go** (or **go-once** for a single tick).

| Parameter | What it controls |
|---|---|
| `wave-budget` | money per wave; a lethal drone costs 100 |
| `decoy-ratio` | % of each wave's budget spent on decoys |
| `decoy-cost` | price of one decoy |
| `attacker-speed` | flight speed of the drones (± 5% random); interceptors fly 1.6 times faster |
| `total-waves`, `wave-interval` | number of waves and ticks between them |
| `sensor-discrimination` | % chance that a base recognises and targets a lethal drone |
| `intercept-accuracy` | % chance that an interceptor destroys its target in clear weather |
| `base-reload-time` | ticks to reload one interceptor |
| `detection-radius` | radar range of a base (the lighter ground) |
| `number-of-bases` | how many bases defend the homeland |
| `decoy-damage` | damage done by a decoy that reaches a base (a lethal drone does 34) |
| `scramble-cooldown-ticks` | minimum ticks between two launches from the same base |
| `rain-chance` | % chance per clear tick that it starts raining |
| `rain-penalty` | % of the kill chance lost while it rains |

The monitors and plots show the weather, bases left, hits and interceptions over time, and a histogram of how far the incoming drones are from their target base.</info>
